    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d245">

                <pb facs="0532" n="502" xml:id="pg502"/>

                <head>245. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Embassy in Korea<anchor n="0" xml:id="d245-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1958-11-12T19:26:00-05:00">November 12, 1958,
                            7:26 p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>185. Re Joint State-Defense message DEF 950561
                    Nov 58.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d245-f2"/> Department understands from Defense that
                    Air Force has instructed jets be placed storage Taiwan Japan maximum six months
                    and eventual delivery ROK will require further
                    Defense instructions. Understand reason for decision was recent CINCUNC message<anchor n="2" xml:id="d245-f3"/>
                    expressing concern force reduction would not be effected if aircraft delivered
                    now. CINCUNC’s concern puzzling in view your
                        174<anchor n="3" xml:id="d245-f4"/> indicating ROK strength may already be at or below 630,000. Defense likewise
                    puzzled and has indicated intention query CINCUNC.</p>
                <p>President has authorized delivery jets and while military at no point have
                    indicated immediate military necessity for presence aircraft ROK, Department has taken consistent position
                    planes should be delivered when ready in view general situation Far East.</p>
                <p>Request your views.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Herter</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d245-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d245-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 795.00/11–1258. Secret; No
                    Distribution Outside Department. Drafted by Lane and approved by Robertson.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d245-f2" n="1" xml:id="d245-f2-content">
                <p><ref target="#d244">Document 244</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d245-f3" n="2" xml:id="d245-f3-content">
                <p>Not found.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d245-f4" n="3" xml:id="d245-f4-content">
                <p>Telegram 174, October 16, commented on President Rhee’s
                    budget message and noted that the existing total strength of the Korean Armed
                    Forces was 610,000 men. Adjusted to include an additional 20,000 reservists, the
                    total did not exceed the 630,000-man ceiling proposed by the United States.
                    (Department of State, Central Files, 895B.10/10–1658) See Supplement.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
